Id: time003i
Severity: INFO
Category: services
Check: check_timesync
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

The clock is synchronised by the daemon named and, for chronyd, from
the server named. This is informational. For a server where the time
matters (logs kept as evidence, Kerberos), chrony with several sources
and Network Time Security (the nts option on a server line) is worth
considering: plain NTP can be spoofed by anyone on the path.
